---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "Privacy", path: "/privacy" },
];
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Devine Plumbing and Heating handles this website. No analytics cookies. The contact form opens a text on your phone and is not stored on a server."
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <div class="wrap page-hero prose">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      This site is for Devine Plumbing and Heating. The phone number is 07436 135412. There is no
      public email on the Google profile, so this page does not invent one.
    </p>
    <h2>What the site stores</h2>
    <p>
      The pages are static. There is no account, no shop, and no analytics tool. We do not set
      tracking cookies. Your browser may still store ordinary files so the pages load faster. That
      is the browser, not an advert profile.
    </p>
    <h2>The text form</h2>
    <p>
      The contact form runs in your browser. It builds a text message to 07436 135412 and asks your
      phone to send it. The words are not posted to a server run by this website. Once you send the
      text, it is a normal message between you and Darren. Keep it only as long as the job needs.
    </p>
    <h2>The map</h2>
    <p>
      The contact page embeds Google Maps. Google receives the fact that your browser loaded the map.
      Their own privacy rules cover that part. The pin is the public Google location. It is not a
      home address published by us.
    </p>
    <h2>Reviews</h2>
    <p>
      Review text on this site is copied from the public Google profile. Names are the names shown
      there. To change or remove a Google review, use Google’s own tools.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
